{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit","id":177379,"title":"The DiFillipo Family, \"The Outfit\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-22T15:19:16-07:00","id":177379,"title":"The DiFillipo Family, \"The Outfit\"","content":"Just my attempt to try and make an organized criminal organization compared to the Night Watch and Ascending Ones.<br /> <br /> Organized crime. The two words immediately brings up images of a group of wise guys gathered around a big Italian dinner, talking about &quot;whacking&quot; someone and making offers that can't be refused. Sadly for organized crime, this image affected them as much as the rest of the world, and in the 70s and 80s images of Italian organized crime families were nearly destroyed by the efforts of the Federal government to dismantle their rackets and organizations. The younger mobsters didn't realize that the stories of the sharply dressed, wise-cracking wise guys were just that; stories. By 1993, La Cosa Nostra (Everyone who does their research knows it's only ever called the Mafia by outsiders) was a shadow, dealing with the invading Mafiya from Eastern Europe, the surge in gang violence by blacks, bikers, and Latinos, and the ever vigilant feds sniffing around.<br /> <br /> The Rafaello Family was such a family, trying to keep itself stable in Albany, NY. The influx of Russians, gangs, and street drugs forced the family into a desperate situation as their brothels and nightclubs were consistently snapped up by other groups. What saved them was the fact that they still held some politicians in one and, and a core team of loyal soldatos and &quot;made men&quot; in the other. Desperate, the boss of the family, Armand &quot;Beltway&quot; Sofia, decided to try and reach out to one of the other criminal organizations in the area for help. Sadly for him, he got it. After a few weeks, rumors were spreading that the boss was acting weird, ordering hits where they had no enemies before and getting their best associates killed or arrested for no reason that would help the family. Some of the men said he was getting pale, others said that he started to act like a junkie in a bad need of a fix. More importantly, one of the made men of the family saw the boss bringing what could only be his mistress into his house, with his wife and children still at home.<br /> <br /> Despite the behavior, the boss' turnaround somehow kept the cops and feds at bay, and the family managed to regain some ground from their competitors by '97. Rumors wouldn't die about the boss though, and eventually Armand had to beat one of the made men down who had been saying the boss didn't have his head on straight anymore. Before anyone could ask questions, they got a job to break up a worker's strike at a nearby construction project. The workers didn't budge when confronted, and the underboss of the family, Tommy &quot;Guts&quot; DiFillipo, ordered as much dirt as possible be dug up. It was a goldmine, the strike leaders dipping their hands into a lot of dirty deals; murders, assaults, arson, everything that would give any anti-labor supporter a hard-on. But the paper trail showed something else. The people they targeted sometimes had no background, no history. Others just seemed to pop out of nowhere. Several disappearances really caught DiFillipo's eye, since the names were associates the boss had said, &quot;Weren't needed anymore&quot;. Digging even deeper (and against the warnings of his fellow made men), DiFillipo found that the money the family was laundering had been sent to the businesses attacked by the strike leaders, and had been attacked long before the family had even started laundering with them. Worried about an attack on the family, DiFillipo tried to call the boss' attention, but was brushed off like he was a child.<br /> <br /> Incensed, DiFillipo gathered his crew and marched them into the boss' home one night, desperate for answers. The found the door unlocked, and moved through the palatial mansion their boss now called a home. There were small spatters of blood over the carpets and hardwood, and the body of a local working girl on the dining room table half-dazed and with a small puddle of blood next to her neck, but no cuts or signs of harm. Guns drawn now, the crew worked their way upstairs. The bedrooms were a mess, and the boss' kids were found knocked out with heavy-duty sleeping pills. The master bedroom was the scene where they found the boss, his wife, and the working girl. Long story short, the working girl turned to ash, the boss and his wife were dead, and a new family formed that night.<br /> <br /> The death of a boss made for big waves, and DiFillipo was forced to answer to the Commission itself, brought to New York and the most secret gathering of the criminal world's leading men, three bosses and two consigleries of New York's Five Families, as well as the underboss of the Chicago Outfit. DiFilllipo tried to avoid the truth knowing that it would probably earn him a bullet to the head and a new iron chain swimsuit, but by the end of the meeting DiFillipo had to face facts: He told the men before him that he killed what could only be a vampire, and that his boss had been it's slave.<br /> <br /> His shock could only be imagined when the men before him admitted they had either known or suspected for years that there were things out there, but that the mob's code of silence had indirectly affected their ability to speak with each other on what they knew. Put simply, no one wanted to openly stick their noses into something that could get themselves killed and their families eliminated. With DiFillipo's actions, the creatures had a new target, but the Commission also saw opportunity. Cosa Nostra had never before tried to play against the monsters for fear of reprisals. Knowing that one of their own had managed to do so, they asked DiFillipo is he thought he could turn the knowledge of monsters into a profit for his family, but for now his family alone. Not seeing any other way out of the meeting, DiFillipo accepted.<br /> <br /> Feelers were slowly spread out to try and figure out just who was what in the new world the family found itself in. For a start, vampires were now trying to eat the family alive by worming in through associates and business partners. There were so many holes in the fence that DiFillipo had to purge hard. Associates were beaten and ordered to leave town, or otherwise disposed of. The cops that could play ball in the local and state police were bribed hard and watched carefully for weeks to ensure they weren't already slaves. Anyone who was had the threat of their dirty secret hung over their heads until they realized their error. The war in Philly covered the family, and soon DiFillipo found himself meeting with the leading vampire of Albany. It was a long, hard negotiation. Just DiFillipo and the vampire. No one knows what happened inside, but the vampire walked out looking half-defeated and ruffled. DiFillipo looked worse, but still alive and his own man. A deal had been breached; the vampires would pay their dues to the family, and in return the family didn't alert the workers to their location.<br /> <br /> DiFillipo realized that the creatures lurking around at night had possibly even more to fear than your average blackmail victim. Their families were sometimes kept completely in the dark, or even didn't know their loved ones were still alive. Their rituals involved strange materials only available through illegal means, or access to locations that only criminals would think of accessing. There was money and favors in that, something DiFillipo knew was more valuable than going around knocking every other monster's head together. Businesses owned by monsters directly or indirectly were strong-armed, the owners reminded that it would be bad for everyone's health if they tried to make a scene. Justifiably afraid of their secrets being found, the rackets started to pick up again. Bootlegged cigarettes, weapons, women, it started to move again, and through the family's hands.<br /> <br /> What didn't pick up was the drug trade. Watching as the Philly mob and others were laid low thanks to the War on Drugs, DiFillipo made the controversial decision to only take the trade from as close to his turf as possible. Local growers, meth cookers, smuggled prescription drugs, less well known and infinitely less dangerous to the family's new situation than the Fed's favorite targets of cocaine and heroin from overseas. Dealers and associates of the family questioned the decision, but DiFillipo stood firm; the weed would be their bulk product, and the rest the moneymakers. It worked for a while, but then someone started going after the dealers. Messages were left, start selling cocaine and heroin again, or else. Knowing he couldn't do anything for now without angering someone apparently powerful enough to evade his police and made men, DiFillipo started selling again, but at much lower rates than the other families on the East Coast.<br /> <br /> More importantly, DiFillipo had other hunters buying his guns, including the workers who had been on strike. Meeting covertly, they explained there were hundreds, maybe thousands of hunters in the world also knowing about the creatures. As a sign of good faith, DiFillipo did give them the guns, but made sure they knew that he was on their side when it came to monsters. Privately, he made sure the men's faces and license plates were photographed. Going to his new protection clients, he flashed their faces, and in a witch's book shop they were pointed out as the ones who nearly beat her to death three months ago for going into their neighborhood. Showing that his family kept their word, the men were arrested and tried on the word of the witch, and the monsters took notice. So did other hunters. Certain groups reached out to the Outfit cautiously, looking for couriers or contracted help for their operations. The monsters started coming for the same; any human that can face down vampires and not blink has something going for them alright.<br /> <br /> Currently DiFillipo is publicly a restauranteur and investor, as well as a local philanthropist to keep himself good looking for the editors and cops on the payroll. Like the old school gangsters, he builds himself up as a man of the people, which to him is somewhat true. He and his men protect them from the creatures in the night. If that means the Outfit takes a bigger piece of the action, all the better. Behind the closed doors, DiFillipo has his men concentrating on three main areas of activity. First is the street level stuff, selling drugs and weapons from the backs of the cars, hooking the monsters and people in the area hooked on what he gives them. Second, telling the monsters who's in charge now. A local pack of werewolves chafed hard at the thought of human criminals telling them who to pay every month, until they saw the DiFillipo had pictures of their homes and loved ones waiting for them. Written on the back of each picture, &quot;Accidents happen&quot;. Some monsters have even begun working as associates for the Outfit, sensing a change in the wind. DiFillipo is happy to go along for now, since a threat against a witch can be easily backed up with a werewolf enforcer. He won't let monsters rise in the organization however. Along with the traditional rule of Italians only, humans are only allowed to become soldiers. There's even a supernatural protection racket, watching over a sacred space or lay line until someone makes a better offer.<br /> <br /> Finally, DiFillipo is trying to make more money from the big player hunters. So far it's led to a few but high-paying jobs; running strange objects from point A to B, acting as contracted muscle for fools in stupid looking jackets or even the Church, and helping the Feds with their more secretive activities. The main goal is to figure out who might be behind the fact that he's been forced to continue dealing drugs he knows will kill his organization.<br /> <br /> <i>(A man wears a suit jacket, slacks, and a button-down shirt with the top button undone. He wears expensive loafers, better than someone his age should have earned. His arms are crossed, he's frowning, but he also has a small leather strap visible on his side, and a wad of bills barely sticking out from his jacket pocket. The shirt is stained in blood, and looks to be a little over 29 years old.)</i><br /> <br /> <b> That's a nice lay line you got there...<br /> It would be a shame if someone...<br /> Built a strip mall over it.</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Competition</b><br /> <br /> No one is an enemy, enemies cause wars. No, there's the &quot;competition&quot;, the ones that you compete against but know better than to fight unless it's necessary. Instead, you're competing with them. You're competing for the best smuggling routes, the best corners, the best clubs and houses. In the shadowy world beyond Cosa Nostra, everyone is a potential competitor.<br /> <br /> The worst are the vampires, who have gotten proud over their abilities to manipulate and control, though witches are a close second. Thinking their powers give them an edge, they move against the Outfit nightly in trying to steal their regained turf. The Outfit fights back by using the daylight to their advantage, telling the police who to stop and where to take them. That's not saying the two can't be negotiated with, indeed the Outfit has so far met with vampires several times to hammer our who controls what and where in the city. Witches have also tried to come at the family as vigilantes, but these flashier witches and wizards don't quite make the leap from &quot;magical superhero&quot; to &quot;automatically bulletproof&quot; sometimes. The ones that do are left to someone that can handle them as the family falls back.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are actually considered good muscle for associates, and this has created a massive schism between the Outfit and any hunters who know. The hunters argue that werewolves are more harm than good, and that trafficking with them will lead to massive damage. The Outfit differs, since 500 pounds of solid muscle is just as desperate for money as the street dealer. Again, not made men at all, the wolves who work with the family do benefit from a better access to sacred spaces without fear of competition, and a steady income when most of their kind have to worry about their rage controlling them in the office.<br /> <br /> Creatures stranger than these are handled on a case-by-case basis. Sometimes a dead man who isn't dead comes walking through, and the family asks him why he's still alive. Good answer, pay a bribe and be on your way. Bad answer, there are some doctors who love getting things like you. A victim's ghost is whispering who did it? The Outfit will call their best exorcist and get that ghost gone, for a steep fee. This serves the dual purpose of finding people who can be convinced that it would be in their very best interests to continue convincing the family not to reveal what happened.<br /> <br /> Other hunters are truly competition, especially groups like the Night Watch out of Pittsburgh. They hate criminals, and the Outfit hates being tread on. Currently the Night Watch won't go out of it's ghettos, and the Outfit makes sure to channel vampires their way to keep them occupied. A more pressing concern is who has forced the family to continue selling crack. What DiFillipo has pieced together is that they operate over a wide area, maybe even into New York, and that they are powerful enough to be involved in opium <i>and</i> cocaine at the same time. DiFillipo is still putting his information together, but knowing someone is manipulating the mob to bring in more money for themselves, it could convince the Commission to act against them and drop the drugs until the Feds cool off and people controlling them stepped down.<br /> <br /> At the same time, competition can give you favors. Hunter groups including the church's Inquisition and government's black ops monster squad have requested aid from the Outfit before, and know enough to repay when the favor is called in after five or ten years. Smaller groups of hunters take the weapons being sold from the Outfit, but are warned point blank that running to the cops will get them arrested and jailed if they're lucky. Others, like fairies, traffic drugs into the city that the Outfit can only imagine using (basic first rule; don't sample the merchandise on yourself). In kind, the Outfit tells them whatever they ask. Some fairies do try and take over Albany's underworld, but they're quickly beaten back down when the family digs in and finds the remaining family of the fairies they're facing off against.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunters</b><br /> <br /> You're an associate, technically not a real part of the family. But you're valuable, in that you're the best numbers runner and bookie in town. You keep track of who's betting on what, and if someone's too lucky to be normal, you know who to point out.<br /> <br /> As a cleaner, you see sick shit every other week. But you've grown numb to it, so when one of the capo's asked you to deal with a new corpse, you didn't think much of it. When you finally managed to dissolve that patchwork <i>thing</i>, you wanted to know just what was going on. Too bad for you, you got the answer.<br /> <br /> The boss wants things done, you do it. Collections, laundering, protecting the girls in the clubs, you do it. Beating witnesses or competitors, you do it. Taking a stake from the weapon's case and finding a priest you can trust, you do it.<br /> <br /> As an old man, you remember the actual mob bosses, you even got to meet &quot;Big Joe&quot; Castellano before that scum Gotti ordered the hit. What you do now is act as mediator, the man the other families can go to when they need a guy for some &quot;special problems&quot; their own can't handle. You have lots of favors for the family now, and when the boss asks, you call them in.<br /> <br /> The days of Murder, Inc. are long gone, but bosses still need hired killers. You provide a service, and that's all it is. Family men, crazed junkies, rapists the bosses don't like, as long as there's money you're in. Usually you don't worry about who your targets were, but somehow, killing monsters seems...right.<br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes<br /> <br /> Ascending Ones:</b> We don't want to do hard drugs because it calls down too much heat. We get suppliers trying to figure out why we're just grabbing from the local meth dealers and pot growers, and sometimes those suppliers get too pushy. A lot of'em have these weird drinks they carry with'em, but no one's dumb enough to drink something that smells like that.<br /> <br /> <b>Network 0:</b> Fucking bloggers think they're hot shit, going around filming everything. We had this one guy, following a crew as they took down this leech's guys, said he wanted to just show the leech existed. Broke his camera, but he was happy to accept our money for a replacement once he realized what we do. Bastard pissed himself too, fucking hilarious.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum:</b> The priests, the Church, they all know. Makes me wonder about John Paul I. Anyway, they usually come from the church three blocks over, ask for Fr. Riviera. They know what we do, but we know what they do. As long as we're sinning for God, I don't think they care what we do.<br /> <br /> <b>Union:</b> Fuckers are still trying to run us down, acting like their shit don't stink. All they keep going on about is &quot;Workers this, workers that&quot;. Bullshit, it's not about the workers for them. They're using the things as a fucking excuse, they can't hack it without stealing the money the things have. How do you think they buy all their guns and shit? They're skimming from the creatures, we're just honest about it.<br /> <br /> <b>Crews</b><b> and Status</b><br /> <br /> The Outfit is organized into three distinct <b>Crews</b>, given no name but what their role in the family is. Each crew is also organized by status in the organization, meaning that only full-human Italians can rise above status 2. Disobey the family or turn against them, and you won't live long enough to know what happens when you lose status.<br /> <br /> <b>SIDEBAR: Monster Mobster<br /> <br /> As mentioned earlier, the Outfit does, in fact, take in creatures as the lowest members of their compact. So are these monsters also hunters?<br /> <br /> Thematically, you can play it either as they are and just ostracized from the compact, or that they aren't and are still ostracized. More importantly, mechanically a creature who is also at status 1 can still use the majority of their abilities. Whether this is a PC or not should be decided beforehand, to iron out which books might be needed for the character(s). They do, however, gain the ability to risk willpower and use tactics like hunters do if your group chooses.<br /> <br /> For the lesser splats (ghouls, wolf-blooded, etc), they function as hunters do for the purposes of willpower, tactics, and hunter merits.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Associates</b> <b>(Status 1)</b> are the compact's informants. Numbers runners, street dealers, all kinds of lowlife scum and malcontents. They don't quite have any power in the group, but are smart enough to realize that the Outfit offers better protection than nearly any other criminals from things that aren't easy to handle, and in return the associates tell the family what's on the streets. Specialty: Criminal Mind: Stealth or Larceny. Someone above you says jump, you jump as high as you can. As a bonus, they might just teach you something worth learning. Treat this as a one-dot mentor in the Outfit.<br /> <br /> <b>Soldiers/Soldato (Status 3) </b>are the &quot;made men&quot; of the compact, Italians who have proven they have what it takes to rise in the family. Governed by a code of silence not seen since Cosa Nostra formed, the Soldiers of the family are the muscle, organizing the hits and killings that the family needs to keep the wolves at bay from the sheep. Specialty: Dirty Fighting: Brawl or Weaponry. You've made your bones, and now can safely say that you have a little pull in the businesses you shakedown for the money. Treat this as Intimidation or Larceny: Racketeering.<br /> <br /> <b>Capos (Status 5) </b>command the soldiers and associates under them, and so act as the leadership of the group. Unlike other compacts, there is a clear message about who's in charge, and disobedience to a capo is often enough to earn severe punishment. Despite this, the capos are also the family's political side, negotiating with the cops and politicians to keep certain noses and ears from where there would be trouble for all involved. Specialty: Offer You Can't Refuse: Intimidation or Persuasion. The Outfit isn't going to risk someone like you breaking kneecaps, so you're in charge of managing the family's finances and interfacing with the local criminal element as well. This usually equates to Allies: Local Criminals, for two dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","user":"Flyboy254","date":". 06-24-2014, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T12:52:01-07:00","id":178142,"title":"","content":"I think what this needs is more profit in monster hunting, and more focus on profit instead of killing monsters. I can understand why selling out to the vampires makes piles of cash, but not why hunting them does so - they might snatch a brothel or a few blocks of turf but it doesn't seem like there's much reason to go after the vast majority who don't have any stake in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of ways to make cash. Running relics for the Ageis Kai Doru or subcontracting for Cherion. Making deals with faeries, whack a fetch and you'll find a little something under your pillow. A Werewolf has been having lots of kids, maybe hire some dowsers and set up a layline protection racket. &quot;You see this here line running from our warehouse to your tranquil grove, wouldn't it be a shame if we put a boxing ring there nice and legal.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Some other thoughts.<br /> <br /> The Commission's reaction didn't feel plausible to me. A group that powerful, either they knew already or they knew already but were in denial. Perhaps they knew but had a policy of not poking any metaphorical sleeping dragons. DiFillipo asked if he could experiment with trying to make a profit from the occult, and the Commission agreed on the condition that it was at arms length from themselves; hence why he has so much freedom.<br /> <br /> The no-drugs policy felt like it was there because the author didn't like drugs. A stronger reason is needed - why would they care if monsters skim provided they're still making a profit? Perhaps once they started moving into the occult business the Jagged Crescent started to boss them around, they said no, so the Crescent cut them off from the supply and sold straight to the dealers. DiFillipo knows better than to pick a fight with the Cartels, and the Commission put him at arms length to prevent exactly this kind of unpleasantness from reaching them. So he wisely backed off.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd generally avoid ever saying a Compact has gotten itself into a Conspiracy's bad books, because that really lowers a Compact's life expectancy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hopefully this will help you make the outfit even better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T14:47:11-07:00","id":178260,"title":"","content":"The drug angle is history: The second the mob got themselves involved in the drug trade, they wound up painting a giant target on their backs. It's what nearly tore the Philly mob to pieces, and it's what led to the rise of the mob's most dangerous competition. If I made it clearer that they don't want to deal in the international drug trade to avoid going down that road again, would it fly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T14:54:52-07:00","id":178262,"title":"","content":"Did the mob in real life abandon the drugs trade? If so I'd make it clear that this is a mob wide and not DiFillipo policy. If not, I'd add something to explain why they're a special case, maybe they don't want two targets - drugs and occult - on their back.<br /> <br /> (Either way, I still don't see why they're cracking down on independent dealers)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T16:41:18-07:00","id":178410,"title":"","content":"No, and I guess this wasn't obvious, they only deal in weed and meth now as mentioned. But this will all be taken under advisement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T21:16:34-07:00","id":178618,"title":"","content":"Just made some edits, hopefully this illustrates the family as more multifaceted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T09:36:56-07:00","id":179800,"title":"","content":"The problem I have with them is... it just seems too likely that, inevitably, one of the supernatural groups would get sick of blackmail and find a way to smash them. Hard.<br /> <br /> What I mean by this is, for example, the Demon the Descent kickstarter mentions a fair number of them in Russia, for example, are quite powerful within the Russian Mafia. My question is what keeps creatures that have similar connections in the U.S. from just crushing this group? Its already been brought up that the La Coka Nostra are hardly the toughest organized crime group anymore, and additionally, I highly doubt that his was the only family at some point infiltrated by say, Vampires.<br /> <br /> My point is, from what I've seen, the supernatural are just undeniably better at organized crime than their human counterparts. The Vampires have literally centuries of experience, connections, ect. to work with, Changeling freeholds, judging by Lords of Summers, frequently have freeholds that are also powerful crime groups from being able to utilize their abilities, and Demons are literally used to hiding from the local setting's equivalent to God. What does this family have on any of that? Why would one of these groups not, at some point, just crush them because they get irritated by having to put up with their blackmail? I understand with local supernatural, but at some point, wouldn't they come across say, a Vampire that has similar connections and would not be willing to put up with their crap?<br /> <br /> My over all point here is it seems you're having a Compact trying to compete with the supernatural in an area where they're just clearly better from what I've seen, and also have almost none of their disadvantages present. Thoughts on this? I hope this is helpful.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For the stuff with Vampires, what incentive do they have to let this human group have any territory at all? They're more powerful, have probably been around longer, and just over all have more power. Considering how strong Blood and Smoke made them, the group would be overwhelmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":". 06-25-2014, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T10:24:26-07:00","id":179835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=179800#post179800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is, from what I've seen, the supernatural are just undeniably better at organized crime than their human counterparts. The Vampires have literally centuries of experience, connections, ect. to work with,</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell no. Changelings are paranoid and alien creatures who usually trouble interacting with people. Demon's aren't much better, and their organised crime networks have a strong tendency to be <i>attacked by god</i>. Vampire's are predatory creatures who are close to pathologically incapable of having an honest positive relationship*. <br /> <br /> Organised crime depends on trust, honesty and reputation in a way that the legal world does not. If you buy a thousand cakes and the company runs off, you can sue them. If you hire a safe cracker and he snitches you to the cops what are you going to do? You're in jail and he's in witness protection. Vampires, Changelings and Demons all have massive problems with trust, and all have issues that make it hard to trust them. At best their supernatural powers allow them to play on even terms with the humans; however it's more likely that their organisations don't spread far beyond what they can personally support with their powers while the humans run massive international criminal conspiracies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * See Danse Macabare original and expanded Anchor rules, you could not have a relationship without one dysfunctional element. Sure human relationships have their faults, but the list in Danse Macabare was far worse than anything you'd expect in the average human relationship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T11:33:00-07:00","id":179884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=179835#post179835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hell no. Changelings are paranoid and alien creatures who usually trouble interacting with people. Demon's aren't much better, and their organised crime networks have a strong tendency to be <i>attacked by god</i>. Vampire's are predatory creatures who are close to pathologically incapable of having an honest positive relationship*.<br /> <br /> Organised crime depends on trust, honesty and reputation in a way that the legal world does not. If you buy a thousand cakes and the company runs off, you can sue them. If you hire a safe cracker and he snitches you to the cops what are you going to do? You're in jail and he's in witness protection. Vampires, Changelings and Demons all have massive problems with trust, and all have issues that make it hard to trust them. At best their supernatural powers allow them to play on even terms with the humans; however it's more likely that their organisations don't spread far beyond what they can personally support with their powers while the humans run massive international criminal conspiracies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * See Danse Macabare original and expanded Anchor rules, you could not have a relationship without one dysfunctional element. Sure human relationships have their faults, but the list in Danse Macabare was far worse than anything you'd expect in the average human relationship.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have two problems with this. <br /> <br /> 1. Organized crime has massive problems with trust as shown in shows like the Wire, where they will kill people just because they MIGHT talk, or might have talked, as an example. That sounds like extremely paranoid and, outside of that world, dysfunctional behavior. You're comparing to average human relationships when average human relationships aren't present in this world. <br /> <br /> 2. The advantages supernatural abilities give in organized crime you are underestimating. Somebody who can have literally centuries of experience dodging legal authorities, knowing how to bribe politicians, ect. are all things that would give them an immense advantage over somebody less experience.<br /> <br /> Your entire argument runs on humans being better at trust when in this type of organization, but I don't see the evidence for that. They're still going to be paranoid, and unlike Changelings for example, who can force you to be more loyal through pledges, they have no ability to use supernatural gifts to insure security. <br /> <br /> To go to your last point, criminals are not the average human relationships. Honesty and trust are not going to be any better than with other supernaturals, because again, they already live in a world where both will be in short supply, along with both frequently needing brute force, or the threat of it, to be enforced. Yes, there are honor codes, but even those aren't comparable to things supernaturals with abilities, like again, Changelings using Pledges to have supernatural enforcement for one's ability to talk, among other things. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T12:45:44-07:00","id":179967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=179884#post179884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Organized crime has massive problems with trust as shown in shows like the Wire, where they will kill people just because they MIGHT talk, or might have talked, as an example. That sounds like extremely paranoid and, outside of that world, dysfunctional behavior. You're comparing to average human relationships when average human relationships aren't present in this world.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to start with all the problems you see on The Wire and then add the monster's innate issues on top. This isn't just my personal point of view, it's right there in the rules. An Elder, like the example you're useing, typically falls around Humanity 3. That's a -3 penalty to all rolls to relate to humans (&quot;relate&quot; is a bit vague I know but the surrounding fluff sounds comprehensive). If you deduct a point to show the difference between a typical Elder and an Elder who lives a life of crime; that's -5.<br /> <br /> <br /> So are humans better at trust than your hypothetical vampire Elder. Three to five dice better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=179884#post179884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. The advantages supernatural abilities give in organized crime you are underestimating. Somebody who can have literally centuries of experience dodging legal authorities, knowing how to bribe politicians, ect. are all things that would give them an immense advantage over somebody less experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between being 100 times as good, and making everyone beneath you ten times as good.<br /> <br /> The bigger the organisation, the better of you are if your skill is in making the people beneath you better. Sure magic can help; but it doesn't scale that well. Changeling's only have so many Pledges to go around - and a low Clarity Changeling is going to have a very hard time meeting lots of people who haven't been pledged yet in order to get their handshake. The skill that really matters is understanding people, understanding them well enough that you can create a culture that brings out their most effective side.<br /> <br /> A mortal mobster might do it, if he's good enough. A Vampire mobster, well it will be shedding Humanity fast and the books explicitly say that without Humanity you don't understand people or care about understanding people.<br /> <br /> As for a demon mobster; they'll do just as well or better than a Mortal, until their association gets big and the G-M notices. Most demons don't invest heavily into one life, they'll probably have to ditch it one day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T13:03:09-07:00","id":179978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=179967#post179967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need to start with all the problems you see on The Wire and then add the monster's innate issues on top. This isn't just my personal point of view, it's right there in the rules. An Elder, like the example you're useing, typically falls around Humanity 3. That's a -3 penalty to all rolls to relate to humans (&quot;relate&quot; is a bit vague I know but the surrounding fluff sounds comprehensive). If you deduct a point to show the difference between a typical Elder and an Elder who lives a life of crime; that's -5.<br /> <br /> <br /> So are humans better at trust than your hypothetical vampire Elder. Three to five dice better.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, with the dice thing, and I'm willing to concede it with Vampires. Changelings I'm more iffy with because, again, counter evidence from Lords of Summer sample freeholds and similar. There are too many that do criminal activities for it to always be something that hurts Clarity, which removes much of the disadvantage. The paranoia of higher Clarity Changelings is very comparable to those of human mobsters, not especially higher considering, again, the massive issues with trust and honesty mobsters constantly have to deal with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a difference between being 100 times as good, and making everyone beneath you ten times as good.<br /> <br /> The bigger the organisation, the better of you are if your skill is in making the people beneath you better. Sure magic can help; but it doesn't scale that well. Changeling's only have so many Pledges to go around - and a low Clarity Changeling is going to have a very hard time meeting lots of people who haven't been pledged yet in order to get their handshake. The skill that really matters is understanding people, understanding them well enough that you can create a culture that brings out their most effective side. </div> </div> </div>The last is something Fairest and the like can be very good at, however, I think I'm getting your point more. Essentially, would it be fair to say that essentially, the creatures immoral enough to do crime you're saying would have problems because their lower morality would penalize their social stats, essentially? If so, that's fair, and something I didn't take into account.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A mortal mobster might do it, if he's good enough. A Vampire mobster, well it will be shedding Humanity fast and the books explicitly say that without Humanity you don't understand people or care about understanding people. </div> </div> </div>This is I would note, once again, is from the same group of people who will frequently act psychopathically in regards to their lower members, but your over all point stands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for a demon mobster; they'll do just as well or better than a Mortal, until their association gets big and the G-M notices. Most demons don't invest heavily into one life, they'll probably have to ditch it one day. </div> </div> </div>This cuts into something. Your argument works, if we assume they were dealing with the entire Mafia, but they aren't. They are dealing with one family, which doesn't have the same resources. Its also worth noting that, in the Kickstarter pdf, many demons had been doing very well in organizations like the Russian Mafia, suggesting the G-M isn't as much a hindrance to their ability to use such organizations as it appears. Therefore, I'd argue, your argument against Demons isn't valid enough to work for this group, especially as, its one family, and therefore, isn't large enough to take advantage of such a scale.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I see your point with Vampires, and with Changelings, depending on the crime. I say depending because, judging by Lords of Summer, as an example, there are clearly crimes that don't hurt Clarity as much, as an example, and they can commit with relative impunity. Vampires I concede the point, although wouldn't many have control of the Russian Mafia if they existed since Rome, or at least have heavy influence on it? I'm sorry I keeping harping on how old they are, but it just seems like something that would constantly come up with this type of conflict.<br /> <br /> <br /> Essentially though, this all depends on either,<br /> A. Morality penalties hurting social ability which doesn't apply to every supernatural splat, and the ones it doesn't would keep the advantage,<br /> B. In the case of Demons, the God Machine acting as a restraining bolt on their ability to grow organizations, which doesn't have enough evidence supporting it from Demon the Descent, judging by the Kickstarter.<br /> C. This particular Compact being large enough to take advantage of the scale advantages you bring up, which I can't see. It is just one family. Yes, families can be quite large in their scope of power, but they don't seem to even be beyond a single city, which is well within the purview of a Freehold, or organizations that Demons can have before the G-M cracks down on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":". 06-25-2014, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T13:27:38-07:00","id":180033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=179978#post179978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, with the dice thing, and I'm willing to concede it with Vampires. Changelings I'm more iffy with because, again, counter evidence from Lords of Summer sample freeholds and similar. There are too many that do criminal activities for it to always be something that hurts Clarity, which removes much of the disadvantage.</div> </div> </div> </div> Petty Theft is Clarity 7, killing a human is Clarity 2. I suspect most other crimes fall somewhere between that.<br /> <br /> Just because it's a really bad idea doesn't mean Changeling's (or others) won't do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=179978#post179978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last is something Fairest and the like can be very good at, however, I think I'm getting your point more.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well a Vampire's problem is the inability to understand or care about human behaviour. A Fairest's problem is going utterly insane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=179978#post179978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially, would it be fair to say that essentially, the creatures immoral enough to do crime you're saying would have problems because their lower morality would penalize their social stats, essentially? If so, that's fair, and something I didn't take into account.</div> </div> </div> </div> It varies by Splat of course. Vampire's get massive disadvantages both from crime and from being a vampire (daysleep).<br /> <br /> Werewolves get their social penalties from Primal Urge rather than Harmony but Werewolves also tend to think in terms of Tier 1 groups; there's no mechanics for that but it's a big deal. (They're getting bigger in the GMC, but more Sons of Anarchy big not Mafia big)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=179978#post179978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is I would note, once again, is from the same group of people who will frequently act psychopathically in regards to their lower members, but your over all point stands.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hence the keyword &quot;good&quot;. Most mobster's couldn't create a Mafia or maintain one if the old Don made them his heir. But with more mortals than monsters; and no drawbacks like Detachment, you're going to see a lot more mortals than vampires with the skill to run a massive criminal syndicate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=179978#post179978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This cuts into something. Your argument works, if we assume they were dealing with the entire Mafia, but they aren't. They are dealing with one family, which doesn't have the same resources.</div> </div> </div> </div> However that is a very recent development.<br /> <br /> The DiFillipo territory was previously Mafia territory. Anything big enough to challenge the Mafia would have been driven out before the family was founded. Now perhaps some demon or vampire is going to see weakness and move in to take the opportunity. But perhaps the DiFillipos are going to make enough profit that the Commission will declare the experiment a huge success; and then it will be the entire Mafia we're dealing with.<br /> <br /> Either way, DiFillipo as a lone isolated Mafia family trying to profit from the supernatural is probably a temporary situation. They key point though, is that temporary is not the same as doomed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=179978#post179978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of Demons, the God Machine acting as a restraining bolt on their ability to grow organizations, which doesn't have enough evidence supporting it from Demon the Descent, judging by the Kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div> Didn't they infiltrate human organisations rather than build their own from the ground up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T13:49:19-07:00","id":180042,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=180033#post180033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Petty Theft is Clarity 7, killing a human is Clarity 2. I suspect most other crimes fall somewhere between that.<br /> <br /> Just because it's a really bad idea doesn't mean Changeling's (or others) won't do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, although that might change if you updated with Integrity style rules, as then, there would be more flexibility with petty theft(one reason I hated the old morality rules, but that's a discussion for another time, and doesn't matter as much anymore anyway.) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well a Vampire's problem is the inability to understand or care about human behaviour. A Fairest's problem is going utterly insane. </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> At this point, I'm not going to argue this point, as I clearly don't know enough about Vampires, and Changelings I'd argue are suffering from using something based on the old Morality rules. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It varies by Splat of course. Vampire's get massive disadvantages both from crime and from being a vampire (daysleep).<br /> <br /> Werewolves get their social penalties from Primal Urge rather than Harmony but Werewolves also tend to think in terms of Tier 1 groups; there's no mechanics for that but it's a big deal. (They're getting bigger in the GMC, but more Sons of Anarchy big not Mafia big) </div> </div> </div>While I definitely don't think Werewolves would compete here, as I agree they're usually small scale, wouldn't their pack culture possibly give them an important advantage over say, traditional gangs? Again, they aren't competing with the mob, as obviously, they can't brute force the situation, but I'm just making an obversation for say, Tier 1 crime. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hence the keyword &quot;good&quot;. Most mobster's couldn't create a Mafia or maintain one if the old Don made them his heir. But with more mortals than monsters; and no drawbacks like Detachment, you're going to see a lot more mortals than vampires with the skill to run a massive criminal syndicate. </div> </div> </div>With Vampires sure, but Demons? No. I bring this up because... well, Demons could matter a lot here. <br /> <br /> [QUOTE]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However that is a very recent development.<br /> <br /> The DiFillipo territory was previously Mafia territory. Anything big enough to challenge the Mafia would have been driven out before the family was founded. Now perhaps some demon or vampire is going to see weakness and move in to take the opportunity. But perhaps the DiFillipos are going to make enough profit that the Commission will declare the experiment a huge success; and then it will be the entire Mafia we're dealing with.<br /> <br /> Either way, DiFillipo as a lone isolated Mafia family trying to profit from the supernatural is probably a temporary situation. They key point though, is that temporary is not the same as doomed. </div> </div> </div>This goes into a massive problem. Namely, I do not buy that the Mafia isn't immensely infiltrated by other supernatural splats. They have been around too long, are too large, and have too many other factors that would them prime for being infiltrated by say, Vampires(not necessarily controlled mind you), and additionally? I don't see how they would clean ranks. This matters because, once again, their scale advantage isn't something that can help them, as now, they have numerous members that might be the very creatures they are trying to hunt. The family perhaps could do this, but that's because its only over one city. The entire organization is a much bigger problem, and might actually be the reason they wanted to let sleeping dogs lie, because they have too many members that could be impacted by such. <br /> <br /> The other issue with this is why I actually don't mind the Night Watch, for example, or the Ascending Ones. The Night Watch are a decentralized organization, therefore, there's no one that there enemies can kill that would massively disrupt it in specific, from what I understand. Meanwhile, the Ascending Ones are a conspiracy, and have their drugs to help them even the odds, along with having diversity by having ties to say, religious organizations, which doesn't leave them the same vulnerabilities. By comparison, the DiFillipo family is centralized, making them far easier to disrupt, and are the size of a Compact. This puts them at a disadvantage, ironically enough, against their more decentralized counterparts I'd argue, as they couldn't recover from blows as well. <br /> <br /> Finally, I'd note that the Mafia has been noted as being far weaker than in the past, including many competitors that are eating away at them. What if those rivals are more flexible with who gets to rise in the ranks if they're a monster or not? I bring this up because that means they're at a major disadvantage against criminal organizations that say, don't mind having Werewolves or Vampires of higher rank. The other reason I note it is I actually like them using monsters as low level members, because it would even the odds against say, creatures rather bullet resistant, and helps post the GMC update making monsters WAY tougher than in the past(I'd note Werewolves are shaping up to be virtually bulletproof in Garou form at times). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Didn't they infiltrate human organisations rather than build their own from the ground up? </div> </div> </div> Sometimes, but other times, its worth noting Messengers, for example, can potentially have quite large cults, possibly easily as large as this particular family. Meanwhile, even those who infiltrate could become high rank enough to have similar levels of power. This matters because, in the case of the Russian Mafia? That organization is WAY more powerful at this point than the La Cosa Nostra, considering how much power they potentially in the Russian government, among other factors. <br /> <br /> My point with this is, at least with Demons, they have no chance. But, to be fair with that, the Unchained probably aren't on their list of targets, all things considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T14:40:20-07:00","id":180097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=180042#post180042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, although that might change if you updated with Integrity style rules, as then, there would be more flexibility with petty theft</div> </div> </div> </div> Changelings crave stability - they have Breaking Points for sudden life changes, no one else has that - so any updated Clarity rules would probably still make it a bad idea for a Lost to go into the high pressure low trust environment of crime.<br /> <br /> (They'd still do it of course)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=180042#post180042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This goes into a massive problem. Namely, I do not buy that the Mafia isn't immensely infiltrated by other supernatural splats.</div> </div> </div> </div> Firstly, what percentage of those infiltrators are working against the Mafia vs working for the Mafia?<br /> <br /> A Mafisio sells his soul to a Demon. Is that Demon going to turn on the Mafia to protect some demon they're blackmailing, or will he stick to his Cover and protect his powerbase from other Demons?<br /> <br /> Secondly a lot of monsters are more likely to place pawns in the mob than to try and take them over completely. After all, that -5 makes it very hard for a vampire to pretend to be human to his subordinates. But a Ghoul doesn't have the powers and experience a Vampire does to keep himself safe if someone thinks he's reporting to the cops.<br /> <br /> Thirdly protecting human institutions from supernatural infiltration is what Hunters do. The Mafia has close ties to the Catholic Church; and the Malleus Maleficarum tend to be more ethically flexible than the rest of the Church. I wouldn't be suprised if prominent Catholics on both side of the law have an agent of the Shadow Congregation planted as their personal priest.<br /> <br /> Forthly, the Mafia is paranoid. They won't get everybody, but they will get some of them.<br /> <br /> Fifthly, if one Vampire manages to subvert a massive criminal organisation. The others might just gang up on him.<br /> <br /> <br /> So no big reason. But lots of little reasons that all add up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=180042#post180042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By comparison, the DiFillipo family is centralized, making them far easier to disrupt, and are the size of a Compact. This puts them at a disadvantage, ironically enough, against their more decentralized counterparts I'd argue, as they couldn't recover from blows as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> But the DiFillipo family are a short term experiment by a much larger group. Either they go down in a few years like you say and the Mafia goes back to it's diminishing business as usual or they work for just long enough, the Comission rolls out their knowledge across the board, and then they bring in their size and economies of scale.<br /> <br /> Endowments are only a small part of what makes Conspiracies scary. Size and organisation are much more useful; though it's not impossible for the Mafia to acquire an Endowment of their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=180042#post180042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, I'd note that the Mafia has been noted as being far weaker than in the past, including many competitors that are eating away at them.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you wanted to say that the Russian Mafia or the feds are a major threat I won't argue. But in real life those groups haven't destroyed the Mafia, yet.<br /> <br /> As for a Messenger with a Family sized cult; clearly there aren't any in the DiFillipo turf at the moment. If they were they would have been noticed before the DiFillipo family went semi-independent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=180042#post180042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes, but other times, its worth noting Messengers, for example, can potentially have quite large cults, possibly easily as large as this particular family. Meanwhile, even those who infiltrate could become high rank enough to have similar levels of power. This matters because, in the case of the Russian Mafia? That organization is WAY more powerful at this point than the La Cosa Nostra, considering how much power they potentially in the Russian government, among other factors.</div> </div> </div> </div> Still though, it's the humans who built the Russian Mafia, Demons are just piggybacking.<br /> <br /> It's easy to hide from the God Machine inside a large human organisation. It's much harder to disguise a large demoniacally created organisation as a human created organisation. It's probably also not the easie<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=180042#post180042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point with this is, at least with Demons, they have no chance. But, to be fair with that, the Unchained probably aren't on their list of targets, all things considered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree that La Cosa Nostra has no chance against the Russian Mafia; but again if the Russian Mafia didn't exist - could Demons build it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-25-2014, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T15:08:36-07:00","id":180110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=180097#post180097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Changelings crave stability - they have Breaking Points for sudden life changes, no one else has that - so any updated Clarity rules would probably still make it a bad idea for a Lost to go into the high pressure low trust environment of crime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but what if they were a criminal before being taken to Arcadia making such stable to them? After all, I remember reading in the book how political bickering was almost like stability to some of them(can't remember the specifics unfortunately,) so that could possibly apply to them if they had a former life of say, being an enforcer, or a thief.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Firstly, what percentage of those infiltrators are working against the Mafia vs working for the Mafia?<br /> <br /> A Mafisio sells his soul to a Demon. Is that Demon going to turn on the Mafia to protect some demon they're blackmailing, or will he stick to his Cover and protect his powerbase from other Demons?<br /> <br /> Secondly a lot of monsters are more likely to place pawns in the mob than to try and take them over completely. After all, that -5 makes it very hard for a vampire to pretend to be human to his subordinates. But a Ghoul doesn't have the powers and experience a Vampire does to keep himself safe if someone thinks he's reporting to the cops.<br /> <br /> Thirdly protecting human institutions from supernatural infiltration is what Hunters do. The Mafia has close ties to the Catholic Church; and the Malleus Maleficarum tend to be more ethically flexible than the rest of the Church. I wouldn't be suprised if prominent Catholics on both side of the law have an agent of the Shadow Congregation planted as their personal priest.<br /> <br /> Forthly, the Mafia is paranoid. They won't get everybody, but they will get some of them.<br /> <br /> Fifthly, if one Vampire manages to subvert a massive criminal organisation. The others might just gang up on him.<br /> <br /> So no big reason. But lots of little reasons that all add up. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, although the Mafia's paranoia seems awfully similar to the type of paranoia Changelings have, undercutting something you said earlier.<br /> <br /> Now, the Catholic Church connection I admit is something to consider, however that goes into the problem of why the Commission wouldn't have tried something like this earlier, and/or, why they seemed hesitant to deal with the supernatural. They come off as going, &quot;this group is expandable, we better make sure this shit doesn't spread.&quot;<br /> <br /> Finally, its worth noting that this entire organization formed because... they were successfully infiltrated by a Vampire. Why would the other families of the Commission do any better than this one?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the DiFillipo family are a short term experiment by a much larger group. Either they go down in a few years like you say and the Mafia goes back to it's diminishing business as usual or they work for just long enough, the Comission rolls out their knowledge across the board, and then they bring in their size and economies of scale.<br /> <br /> Endowments are only a small part of what makes Conspiracies scary. Size and organisation are much more useful; though it's not impossible for the Mafia to acquire an Endowment of their own. </div> </div> </div>I guess part of my issue really just comes from not getting the Commission, or how say, the other families are doing in regards to the supernatural. For some reason, they haven't intervened before hand, which I guessed was because they didn't want to rock boats with the supernatural for some reason. Now, perhaps I'm wrong in that, but I want to get across part of where I'm coming from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you wanted to say that the Russian Mafia or the feds are a major threat I won't argue. But in real life those groups haven't destroyed the Mafia, yet. </div> </div> </div>Yes, however in this case, you may have supernaturals wanting to use aspects of those organizations to enhance their own efforts to smash this particular family, or at least force it to back off. That's what I meant way back by say, Vampires having connections.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still though, it's the humans who built the Russian Mafia, Demons are just piggybacking.<br /> <br /> It's easy to hide from the God Machine inside a large human organisation. It's much harder to disguise a large demoniacally created organisation as a human created organisation. It's probably also not the easie<br /> <br /> I would agree that La Cosa Nostra has no chance against the Russian Mafia; but again if the Russian Mafia didn't exist - could Demons build it? </div> </div> </div>This I'd argue is screwed with by what we know about Demons in Hong Kong, such as the ones who have access to an entire freaking prison they can use to have virtually unlimited burn covers. From what I remember, they didn't piggyback on anyone to create that organization. For another comparison, again, consider Cults formed around Messenger angels. What would it be like if a Messenger Angel decided to utilize a cult of human followers to make life miserable for this particular family? Even with the help of Catholic Hunters, they would find themselves fighting an opponent they can't consistently identify, and many possibly fanatical followers trying to disrupt them.<br /> <br /> For that one actually, imagine what a Messenger Angel could do by pretending to be an Angel from Catholic scripture. Granted, this is now more a weakness for other Hunter groups, but it applies to this one if they have heavy ties to the Catholic Church.<br /> <br /> In hindsight, I think some of my issue comes from seeing the La Cosa Nostra as too weak and, in some ways, inflexible considering they won't allow monsters to advance higher, denying themselves a powerful advantage. I'd actually probably be more forgiving if either,<br /> <br /> A. They were much more flexible with who got to be soldiers, among other things, which obviously the La Cosa Nostra isn't going to be, or,<br /> <br /> B. Were a more powerful organized crime group, like say the Russian Mob, or similar, rather than one that is specifically noted for being in decline.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T15:18:56-07:00","id":180118,"title":"","content":"I'd like to jump in and note that, for the mob, saying a vampire took your boss as a slave is like saying, &quot;I'm the reincarnation of Jimmy Hoffa, my body is under the World Trade Center&quot; level of crazy. The Commission can't afford to be that yet, but an entire family that knows, and has some supernatural muscle and favors to call in, that's a damn good start to avoiding trouble. Even if vampires subverted a few wise guys, the werewolf associates are going to smell something off when Jimmy the Fish starts acting weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T15:30:08-07:00","id":180122,"title":"","content":"Ah, interesting. Okay, that solves some issues I have with this, although this begs, why not let Werewolves get higher in rank? Not saying they should be high ranking per say, but why can't they at least be Soldiers(perhaps I misunderstand the full implications of being a Soldier)? I comment on this as I really like the idea of an organization being willing to use monsters as muscle, but the Mafia here seems to pointlessly limiting itself by not taking full advantage of Werewolves, who I'd note one doesn't have to worry about infiltration as much with as say, Vampires, who they would rightly fear with that. <br /> <br /> But the issue is, wouldn't this problem have come up earlier? I can't imagine Vampires exactly avoid interactions with groups like the Mafia, so shouldn't have past bosses been made slaves too?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T16:02:58-07:00","id":180138,"title":"","content":"Cosa Nostra only allows full-blood Italians to rise in the ranks at all, and if you're a hunter you're already suspicious of monsters anyway. Monster can be associates because the associates are often the first ones arrested, but can't bring down the whole organization if they are. It also means associates who are also monsters need to show even more loyalty, or else they might not get bailed out of jail.<br /> <br /> Depends on where the vampire made the slave in the organization. If they went for a few made men or associates, there's no need for the boss to be a slave, because the lower guys are doing the dirty work. But in essence, in this situation? <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MST3KMantra\" target=\"_blank\">Recite the mantra.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T16:21:32-07:00","id":180150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=180138#post180138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cosa Nostra only allows full-blood Italians to rise in the ranks at all, and if you're a hunter you're already suspicious of monsters anyway. Monster can be associates because the associates are often the first ones arrested, but can't bring down the whole organization if they are. It also means associates who are also monsters need to show even more loyalty, or else they might not get bailed out of jail.<br /> <br /> Depends on where the vampire made the slave in the organization. If they went for a few made men or associates, there's no need for the boss to be a slave, because the lower guys are doing the dirty work. But in essence, in this situation? <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MST3KMantra\" target=\"_blank\">Recite the mantra.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, the solution to all problems relating to continuity or logical errors ever.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But for the first, oh! No wonder they're in decline, they have an artificial disadvantage compared to organizations with more... liberal policies regarding who gets to rise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T16:23:32-07:00","id":180153,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind, those other organizations also tear themselves apart every few years from the inside because there's something they can pick apart and fight over.<br /> <br /> Indeed. But seriously, if you ask how the mob has survived in a world with vampires for as long as the mob has been around, you're gonna have to handwave a few things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T16:59:42-07:00","id":180180,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=180153#post180153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind, those other organizations also tear themselves apart every few years from the inside because there's something they can pick apart and fight over.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, true. So, in that sense, I guess the Loca Nostra aren't really that unique in that respect. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Indeed. But seriously, if you ask how the mob has survived in a world with vampires for as long as the mob has been around, you're gonna have to handwave a few things. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, although I think you could use their connections to say, the Catholic Church, to solve some of these problems. I don't think this necessarily requires a hand wave, but hey, do what you want. Most of my issues with this have been resolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T07:22:48-08:00","id":359105,"title":"","content":"May I make a suggestion Flyboy.<br /> <br /> I was rereading this old thread and I noticed that you've merged Crews and Status - I'm not sure that's appropraite for this group. What you have at the moment for Status looks great but I'd suggest adding the traditional three subgroups as well. As a rough idea:<br /> <br /> Specialists - Tier 1 Hunters, members of the Union, and other associated oddballs or monsters who've been doing this for longer than the Outfit. The Family takes them in, gives them support, access to the Family's black market supply lines: military grade weapons, grave dirt from Transylvania, fall guys for the cops, special dispensation to take a group with you once you find the vampire who killed your family. In return they train the Outfit's soldiers and kill whatever monster the outfit tells them to kill.<br /> <br /> Local Boys - The outfit's social experts. If a mage wants something stolen from a Museum in Italy a Local Boy cuts the deal. If it's time to invite all the cops in your pocket to a party local boys arrange everything. Public relations with the people living in your territory, that's the Local Boys job.<br /> <br /> Enforcers - The normal fighters in contrast to the Specialists. The sort of muscle men you'd expect to see in real life Mafia outfits, with some training from Socialists to top things of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T09:49:31-08:00","id":359245,"title":"","content":"As a side note, one of my uncles has the last name DiFillipo.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really <i>mean</i> anything, it just made this entire thread kinda cognitively-dissonant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T23:04:39-08:00","id":359912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/177379-the-difillipo-family-the-outfit?p=180138#post180138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cosa Nostra only allows full-blood Italians to rise in the ranks at all, and if you're a hunter you're already suspicious of monsters anyway. Monster can be associates because the associates are often the first ones arrested, but can't bring down the whole organization if they are. It also means associates who are also monsters need to show even more loyalty, or else they might not get bailed out of jail.</div> </div> </div> </div>My main money wrench into this is why would supernaturals remain within the Cosa Nostra within a extended period of time if they never get any status out of it? Eventually, someone will make a power play or they'll go off from &quot;our thing&quot; to do &quot;their thing&quot; like how any other business model works. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T00:40:01-08:00","id":359979,"title":"","content":"I guess the same reason real life non-Italian members stick with the mob.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}